---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const labUrl = import.meta.env.LAB_URL || 'http://localhost:4173/';
---
<div class="sm-hero-copy">
  <p class="sm-eyebrow">EMBEDDABLE CRDTS, RUST CORE.</p>
  <h1 id="_top" class="sm-hero-tagline">Offline edits.<br /><span>Predictable merges.</span></h1>
  <p class="sm-hero-lead">Merge counters and sets across disconnected replicas. SafeMesh handles the merge rules; your application supplies transport and storage.</p>
  <div class="sm-hero-actions">
    <a class="sm-button sm-button-primary" href={`${base}/getting-started/#rust-gold-path`}>Start with Rust <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    <a class="sm-text-link" href={labUrl}>Try failure modes ↗</a>
  </div>
  <p class="sm-hero-note">Build from source, no Lean setup required</p>
  <p class="sm-languages">Rust, TypeScript/WASM, Python, C<br /><a href={`${base}/using-safemesh/`}>Compare language capabilities →</a></p>
</div>
